      "header": "Panel A — Spherocytes (Warm AIHA)",
      "content": [
        {
          "library": "H5P.Text 1.1",
          "params": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Spherocytes</strong>: small, round, densely-stained RBCs that have <strong>lost their central pallor</strong> (membrane removed by splenic macrophages after IgG coating). Hallmark of <strong>warm autoimmune haemolytic anaemia</strong> (and hereditary spherocytosis). Confirm AIHA with a positive <strong>direct antiglobulin test (DAT/Coombs)</strong>.</p>"
          },
          "subContentId": "f7484987-9671-4bc9-8a41-ca645227ec62",
          "metadata": {
            "contentType": "Text",
            "license": "U",
            "title": "Panel A — Spherocytes (Warm AIHA)"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "position": {
        "x": 75,
        "y": 32,
        "legacyPositioning": false
      },
      "alwaysFullscreen": false,
      "hotspotIconType": "icon",
      "hotspotIcon": "plus",
      "hotspotColor": "#a4154b",
      "header": "Panel B — Schistocytes (MAHA)",
      "content": [
        {
          "library": "H5P.Text 1.1",
          "params": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Schistocytes</strong>: jagged RBC fragments, helmet cells and triangular forms — mechanically sheared. Indicate <strong>microangiopathic haemolytic anaemia (MAHA)</strong>: TTP, HUS, DIC, malignant hypertension, mechanical valves. Look for accompanying <strong>thrombocytopenia</strong>; the DAT is negative (non-immune).</p>"
          },
          "subContentId": "8f4a13fb-5825-4be1-844a-ea5f11b4c9ba",
          "metadata": {
            "contentType": "Text",
            "license": "U",
            "title": "Panel B — Schistocytes (MAHA)"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "position": {
        "x": 25,
        "y": 72,
        "legacyPositioning": false
      },
      "alwaysFullscreen": false,
      "hotspotIconType": "icon",
      "hotspotIcon": "plus",
      "hotspotColor": "#a4154b",
      "header": "Panel C — Bite Cells (G6PD / oxidative)",
      "content": [
        {
          "library": "H5P.Text 1.1",
          "params": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Bite cells (degmacytes)</strong>: RBCs with one or two semicircular 'bites' removed where splenic macrophages pluck out <strong>Heinz bodies</strong> (denatured oxidised haemoglobin). Seen in <strong>G6PD deficiency</strong> during oxidative stress (drugs, infection, fava beans). Blister cells may accompany.</p>"
          },
          "subContentId": "92a4680a-8d1d-4085-835d-f62cd8a8edb5",
          "metadata": {
            "contentType": "Text",
            "license": "U",
            "title": "Panel C — Bite Cells (G6PD / oxidative)"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "position": {
        "x": 75,
        "y": 72,
        "legacyPositioning": false
      },
      "alwaysFullscreen": false,
      "hotspotIconType": "icon",
      "hotspotIcon": "plus",
      "hotspotColor": "#a4154b",
      "header": "Panel D — RBC Agglutination (Cold AIHA)",
      "content": [
        {
          "library": "H5P.Text 1.1",
          "params": {
            "text": "<p>Irregular <strong>clumps</strong> of red cells stuck together — <strong>agglutination</strong> by IgM cold antibodies (cold autoimmune haemolytic anaemia, Mycoplasma, EBV). Distinguish from <em>rouleaux</em> (orderly stacks, seen with high protein/myeloma). DAT is positive for <strong>C3d</strong> (complement).</p>"
          },
          "subContentId": "f707d549-eded-4f1d-968b-f2c1d9671999",
          "metadata": {
            "contentType": "Text",
            "license": "U",
            "title": "Panel D — RBC Agglutination (Cold AIHA)"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
